  "status": "completed",
  "result": "Found Jonnard et al. comparison showing WDS typically has lower dispersion than EDS (0.4-1% RSD for WDS vs 0.4-2% RSD for EDS). Found Seidel et al. showing EDXRF vs spark-OES comparisons on aluminum alloys with specific deviations reported.",
  "evaluation": "Good comparative data obtained, though most is for other alloy systems rather than aluminum-specific"
}"}

{"plan_objective_id": 4, "updated_plan_objective_json": "{
  "id": 4,
  "objective": "Find EDS comparisons with other techniques (XRF, LIBS, spark OES) on specific aluminum alloy samples",
  "rationale": "Alternative analytical techniques provide additional independent composition measurements for validation",
  "status": "completed",
  "result": "Found Seidel et al. (2021) comprehensive study comparing EDXRF, WDXRF, LIBS, and spark-OES on commercial aluminum alloys including certified reference materials. Spark-OES showed <10% relative error for >0.1 wt% elements. LIBS performed better than XRF for light elements like Mg, Si in Al matrices.",
  "evaluation": "Good quantitative comparison data obtained for aluminum alloys from multiple techniques"
}"}

{"plan_objective_id": 8, "updated_plan_objective_json": "{
